+**AC-2 — provisioning present passes the floor and the gate; provisioning absent is BLOCKED.** MET.
+Two throwaway repositories in the scratchpad, each with a real `git worktree`, a manifest, and the
+floor `test -f node_modules/x/a`.
+
+Case A, `provision_command: mkdir -p node_modules/x && touch node_modules/x/a`:
+
+```
+$ register-lane --isolation worktree --manifest <m> ...
+{ "preexisting": 1,
+  "provision": { "command": "mkdir -p node_modules/x && touch node_modules/x/a", "rc": 0, "seconds": 0.009 } }
+
+$ (cd <worktree> && test -f node_modules/x/a) -> floor: PASS (exit 0)
+$ cat preexisting/w1.txt
+e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855  node_modules/x/a
+
+$ gate-receipt --mode worktree ...
+{ "verdict": "pass", "changed": ["src/work.txt"], "allowed": ["src/**"], "violations": [] }
+```
+
+The floor passes because the dependency is really there, and `node_modules` is absent from `changed`
+because the snapshot subtracted it.
+
+Case B, the same job with `provision_command` absent, installing its own `node_modules`:
+
+```
+{ "verdict": "blocked",
+  "changed": ["node_modules/x/a", "src/work.txt"],
+  "allowed": ["src/**"],
+  "violations": ["node_modules/x/a"] }
+```
+
+The subtraction is the snapshot's, never the path's name.
